# Generated books, and the HTML and PDF fragments produced while rendering them.
#
# Nothing here is ever meant to be fetched directly. The Providence rewrite
# rules only apply to paths that do not exist on disk, so a real file in this
# directory is served by Apache as-is, and its name is guessable: a finished
# catalogue lands on book-<book_id>-job-<job_id>.pdf, two small integers. Every
# book generated by the plugin was therefore readable by anyone, with no
# authentication at all — while the same plugin was carefully checking a CSRF
# token before letting a logged-in editor start the generation.
#
# Downloads go through GenerationController::Download(), which checks the user
# and the job before streaming the file. That is the only way in.
#
# Apache 2.4
<IfModule mod_authz_core.c>
    Require all denied
</IfModule>

# Apache 2.2
<IfModule !mod_authz_core.c>
    Order allow,deny
    Deny from all
</IfModule>
